From f441d38babb3596b9cd2d57f13a9943c513493e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:05:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: a tool's own controller number, posted as T/H

A tool had no number of its own: the post wrote T/H as the tool's 1-based
position in the document's tool list, so a shop whose tool table knows the
cutter as T31 got "T1 M6 / G43 H1" - on a Tormach 770MX (#131) that loaded
tool 1's length and ran ~1.5 in high; a shorter H1 would have cut too deep.

- ToolDef gains number: Option<u32>. ChangeTool keeps it either way;
  DeleteTool and DeleteEntity restore it on undo.
- SetToolNumber sets or clears it (undoable), refusing an unknown or
  non-tool name, numbers outside 1-99999, a number another tool already
  has, and a no-op.
- The project file carries an optional "number" on the tool record
  (written only when set; absent = unnumbered, every older file's meaning;
  no version step). A stated number outside 1-99999 is refused on load.
- app::tool_numbers holds the one numbering rule: a tool's own number,
  else its list position (so unnumbered documents post exactly as before),
  and the clash law - two tools of one program that would post the same
  number refuse to post, naming both.
- The tool editor shows "Tool number (0 = list position)"; Apply / Add tool
  queue a SetToolNumber when it changed. tool_editor snapshot updated.

Fixes #221

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
